    314  f100
    315  f100							; --- E4 moth body (bank2 free space $F008-$F9D8) -------------------------
    316  f100							; Entered from bank0 via the $FEF0 entry tramp (sta $1FF8 lands on the
    317  f100							; jmp below at $FEF3). Exits via `jmp MothExitPad` ($FC49): bank2 runs
    318  f100							; sta $1FF6, bank0 serves jmp UE_Next. Rules:
    319  f100							;   - NEVER jsr FoldIndirect or any bank0 routine (a fold from inside
    320  f100							;     bank2 would switch away mid-routine = frozen player).
    321  f100							;   - Enemy records ARE here (org $F9D9) — read directly, no fold needed.
    322  f100							;   - Keep the whole routine inline (no jsr): tramps are tail jmps so
    323  f100							;     the stack depth equals the UE body (+0 vs the $F8 guard).
    324  f100							;   - ZP (rect cache, EnemyRam*, EnemyDataLo/Hi) is RAM: bank-independent.
