   2135  fe9c							; OvShutBand — shutter kill on the PHMOverlay miss path (vcrunch_shutter_plan
   2136  fe9c							; Phase B). Entered from PHMOverlay .OvBand (right-column + player-band
   2137  fe9c							; overlap). The punched cell no longer trips the PF cell walk, so the overlay
   2138  fe9c							; path IS the kill trigger: MetaB b7 (convert's shutter flag) gates it; plain
   2139  fe9c							; D6 strip rooms (b7 clear) fall through to plain solid (old .OvBand
   2140  fe9c							; behavior). Kill follows the VISIBLE right-half block only (async ruling
   2141  fe9c							; 2026-10-14 — the left mirror was removed to fix flicker). Where the
   2142  fe9c							; block is closed but the player is not crunched, VCS3 returns SOLID —
   2143  fe9c							; the walk blocks (no walking through a closed shutter, user
   2144  fe9c							; 2026-10-14b); only the aperture at the player's Y is passable.
   2145  fe9c							; Kill = EnemyDeadMask b7 latch (once per room visit — EnterRoom zeroes) +
   2146  fe9c							; Temp b7 -> kernel hot-bump -> LoseLife; latched = wall REMOVED (open
   2147  fe9c							; hole — VcrShutter punches-only and disarms BandTab; no re-kill).
